void bc_eval_result_free(bc_eval_result_t *r);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Frees the heap\-allocated strings in a \f[CR]bc_eval_result_t\f[R]
structure that was populated by \f[CR]bc_eval(3)\f[R].
Specifically, it frees \f[CR]r\->stdout_data\f[R] and
\f[CR]r\->stderr_data\f[R] using \f[CR]bc_free(3)\f[R] and sets both
pointers to NULL.
.PP
The function does \f[B]not\f[R] free the \f[CR]bc_eval_result_t\f[R]
structure itself, since it is typically stack\-allocated.
.PP
It is safe to call \f[CR]bc_eval_result_free\f[R] with a NULL argument;
the function returns immediately without action.
It is also safe to call it on a zero\-initialized structure (both fields
NULL).
.PP
The \f[CR]bc_eval_result_t\f[R] structure:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]typedef\f[R] \f[B]struct\f[R] {
    char *stdout_data;   \f[I]/* malloc\(aqd stdout output (NUL\-terminated) */\f[R]
    char *stderr_data;   \f[I]/* malloc\(aqd stderr output (NUL\-terminated) */\f[R]
    int   exit_code;     \f[I]/* command exit status ($?) */\f[R]
} bc_eval_result_t;
